From da86afda69d95d6f48d7a665ed736e61351929b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 12:50:05 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] docs, src, tests: name clusters by their code names,
 described as systems

Cluster mentions now follow the platform-naming ruling. Kaiju is the RSES
kaiju platform, described once per document from the facts in
hpc-cluster-setup.md (a Slurm system of 8 compute nodes, each with 104 CPUs,
Intel Xeon Gold 6230R), and Gadi is NCI's Gadi at its first mention in a
document. Identifiers stay as they are: the UW_CLUSTER values, the install
and job-script names, and the container image tags.

Text only: in the Python and Cython files only comments and docstrings
change (token streams with comment and string contents blanked are
identical; ASTs with docstrings and strings stripped are identical).

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
